From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:35:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp: take a retained J713 PMP through a
 firmware suspend

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 720ef40fd0fcd4f9dc081fddb7023f3e0d82318a)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp-export.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-export.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-export.c
index 195452b8f0..25629d0581 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-export.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-export.c
@@ -201,9 +201,6 @@ static int apple_pmp_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 
 	if (!pm_suspend_via_firmware())
 		return 0;
-	/* Retained power votes have no teardown. */
-	if (apple_pmp_display_retained_board())
-		return -EBUSY;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&pmp_lock);
 	if (pmp_device != dev || pmp_asleep)
-- 
2.43.0

